# A174 — a send the engine did not take keeps the moderator's draft (2026-09-15)

## The refusal is real, and its text is worth keeping the draft for
# A private engine on a spare port, one message of 3 000 characters:
$ chatbots-cli --serve --transport http --port 7811 &
$ curl -s -o - -w 'HTTP %{http_code}\n' -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
      -d "{\"text\": \"$(python3 -c 'print("x"*3000)')\"}" http://127.0.0.1:7811/api/message
HTTP 409 {"error":"a message is limited to 2000 characters"}

# `api.post` throws on that, and `run` answered nothing before this change, so `send` had already
# emptied the box by then. With no engine listening the request never leaves the page at all, which is
# the second way the text was lost.

## The page: five wiring checks, against both versions
$ node tools/check-web-deltas.js          # with the old web/app.js
  FAIL  the command helper reports whether the engine took the command
  FAIL  the page posts the message before it empties the box
  FAIL  and it empties the box only when the send was accepted
  FAIL  so that what is typed during the request is not thrown away
  FAIL  and a second Return cannot post the same text twice
5 deltas check(s) failed

$ node tools/check-web-deltas.js          # with the fix
  ok    the command helper reports whether the engine took the command
  ok    the page posts the message before it empties the box
  ok    and it empties the box only when the send was accepted
  ok    so that what is typed during the request is not thrown away
  ok    and a second Return cannot post the same text twice
all deltas checks passed

## The Mac app: the same six tests, against both behaviours
# Mutation: `deliverModeratorDraft` clears the draft regardless of the outcome, which is what the
# controller did before the change.
$ swift test --filter ModeratorDraftTests
  ✘ Test "With no engine the draft stays and the reason is shown" recorded an issue:
    Expectation failed: controller.moderatorDraft == "Is this still here?"
  ✘ Test "The button's action is the same path, not a second one beside it" recorded an issue:
    Expectation failed: controller.moderatorDraft == "Typed once"
  ✘ Test run with 6 tests in 1 suite failed after 0.003 seconds with 2 issues.

$ swift test --filter ModeratorDraftTests     # with the fix
  ✔ Test run with 6 tests in 1 suite passed after 0.003 seconds.

# The two that fail under the mutation are the ones that exercise a send the engine did not take.
# The other four pin the rule itself: cleared on success, kept on refusal, and what was typed while
# the request was in flight is never cleared with it.

